  "body": "An ordinary caller can finish normally after two registered writers update separate descriptor objects and the caller observes their fields and copies the displaced bytes. The supported no-tail and `unit`-tail forms reuse the existing whole-entry and loan cleanup checks.\n\nThe measured cases use a current-field Copy, a mixed-position named literal, or a displaced-byte Copy at matching field positions. Each generates byte-identical C17 to the corresponding explicit `return unit;` source. The previously adopted first-snapshot route with explicit Return emits the same C17 as #1797. A normal-completion snapshot, a mismatched-position displaced Copy and a stale current-field Copy refuse at C17. Lexical escape refuses at CHECK.\n\n- On frozen Gate0, the three ordinary endings reached CHECK and refused at C17 on both original pins. The first private candidate repeated those refusals. The final measurement is on the integrated commit below. [FIRST](https://github.com/wakairo/NewLang_Compiler/issues/1798#issuecomment-7161693904) · [LOCAL READY](https://github.com/wakairo/NewLang_Compiler/issues/1798#issuecomment-7162090442)\n- GCC Release and Clang ASan/LSan+UBSan each passed 11 selected tests. Native passed 70/70 and the well-factored C control passed 35/35. The existing rollback sweep exercised 1,440 CHECK failures, 16 entry-seal failures and 2,236 named C17 failures per output state per profile, checking restoration, retry and output preservation. [Evidence](https://github.com/wakairo/NewLang_Evidence/tree/3bad22a940b0255b613167a1c07a21f6b4b1de47/p1798/gate0)\n- Exact HEAD `74ff94c7d24f702823f0885f8525c7472b2c9cf6`, tree `4e3a7c5dfb3612ecb8de9ddefcfcfbd8e432eed0`, sole parent `94eb75c3efa91a3feb2a14319d840bc00677bed9`. Full-index diff 10 paths, 17,701 B, SHA-256 `6b3532a80a4e29176b7147e95c980abcd66c3970e1bd68738a323a19f57dd1ba`. [DRAFT GO](https://github.com/wakairo/NewLang_Compiler/issues/1798#issuecomment-7162122436)\n\nRefs #1798.",
